      "question_text_candidate": "12.\n[Maximum mark: 18]\nLet zn be the complex number defined as zn = (n2 + n + 1) + i for n ∈  .\n(a)\n(i)\n\u0007Find arg (z0) .\n(ii)\nWrite down an expression for arg (zn) in terms of n .\b\n[3]\nLet wn = z0 z1 z2 z3 ... zn-1 zn for n ∈  .\nfor a , b ∈ + , ab < 1 .\n(b)\n(i)\n\u0007Show that arctan\narctan\narctan\na\nb\na\nb\nab\n( ) +\n( ) =\n+\n−\n\n\n\n\n1\n(ii)\nHence or otherwise, show that arg (w1) = arctan (2) .\b\n[5]\n(c)\nProve by mathematical induction that arg (wn) = arctan (n + 1) for n ∈  .\b\n[10]\n\b\nReferences:\n© International Baccalaureate Organization 2022",
