      "question_text_candidate": "12.\n[Maximum mark: 17]\n(a)\nFind the binomial expansion of (cos q + i sin q)5 . Give your answer in the form a + bi\nwhere a and b are expressed in terms of sin q and cos q . \b\n[4]\n(b)\nBy using De Moivre’s theorem and your answer to part (a), show\nthat sin 5q ≡ 16 sin5q - 20 sin3q + 5 sin q . \b\n[6]\n(c)\n(i)\n\u0007Hence, show that\n5\nand 3\n5\nare solutions of the\nequation 16 sin4q - 20 sin2q + 5 = 0 .\n3\n(ii)\nHence, show that sin\nsin\n5\n5\n5\n4\n.\b\n[7]\n\b\nPlease do not write on this page.\nAnswers written on this page\nwill not be marked.",
      "markscheme_text_candidate": "12.\n(a)\nattempt to expand using binomial theorem:\n(M1)\nNote: Award (M1) for seeing at least one term with a product of a binomial\ncoefficient, power of isinθ and a power of cosθ .\n(\n)\n5\n5\n5\n4\n5\n2\n3\n2\n1\n2\ncos\nisin\ncos\nicos\nsin\ni cos\nsin\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\n+\n=\n+\n+\nC\nC\n5\n3\n2\n3\n5\n4\n4\n5\n5\n3\n4\ni cos\nsin\ni cos sin\ni sin\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\n+\n+\n+\nC\nC\nA1\n(\n)\n(\n)\n5\n3\n2\n4\n4\n2\n3\n5\ncos\n10cos\nsin\n5cos sin\ni 5cos\nsin\n10cos\nsin\nsin\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\n=\n−\n+\n+\n−\n+\nA1A1\nNote: Award A1 for correct real part and A1 for correct imaginary part.\n[4 marks]\n(b)\n(\n)\n5\ncos\nisin\ncos5\nisin5\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\n+\n=\n+\n(A1)\nequate imaginary parts:\n(M1)\n4\n2\n3\n5\nsin5\n5cos\nsin\n10cos\nsin\nsin\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\n=\n−\n+\nA1\nsubstitute\n2\n2\ncos\n1 sin\nθ\nθ\n= −\n(M1)\n(\n)\n(\n)\n2\n2\n3\n2\n5\nsin5\n5 1 sin\nsin\n10sin\n1 sin\nsin\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\n=\n−\n−\n−\n+\nA1\n(\n)\n(\n)\n2\n4\n3\n2\n5\nsin5\n5 1\n2sin\nsin\nsin\n10sin\n1 sin\nsin\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\n=\n−\n+\n−\n−\n+\nA1\n5\n3\n16sin\n20sin\n5sin\nθ\nθ\nθ\n=\n−\n+\nAG\nNote: Some of this working may be seen in part (a). Allow for awarding marks in\npart (b).\n[6 marks]\ncontinued…\n– 26 –\n8823 – 7106M\nQuestion 12 continued\n(c)\n(i)\nfactorising\n5\n3\n16sin\n20sin\n5sin\nθ\nθ\nθ\n−\n+\nM1\n(\n)\n(\n)\n4\n2\nsin5\nsin\n16sin\n20sin\n5\nθ\nθ\nθ\nθ\n=\n−\n+\nEITHER\nR1\nπ\nsin5\n0\n5\n\n=\n\n\n\n\nand\n3π\nsin5\n0\n5\n\n=\n\n\n\n\nNote: The R1 is independent of the M1.\nOR\nsolving sin5\n0\nθ =\nπ\n5\nθ = k\nwhere ∈\nk\n\nR1\nNote: The R1 is independent of the M1.\nTHEN\ntherefore either sin\n0\nθ =\nOR\n4\n2\n16sin\n20sin\n5\n0\nθ\nθ\n−\n+\n=\nπ\nsin\n0\n5 ≠\nand\n3π\nsin\n0\n5 ≠\n(or only solution to sin\n0\nθ =\nis\n0\nθ =\n)\nR1\nare solutions of\n4\n2\n16sin\n20sin\n5\n0\nθ\nθ\n−\n+\n=\nAG\ntherefore π 3π\n,\n5\n5\nNote: The final R1 is dependent on both previous marks.\ncontinued…\n– 27 –\n8823 – 7106M\nQuestion 12 continued\n(ii)\nMETHOD 1\nattempt to use quadratic formula:\n(M1)\n2\n20\n80\nsin\n32\nθ\n±\n=\nA1\n5\n5\n8\n±\n=\n5\n5\nsin\n8\nθ\n±\n=\nπ\n3π\n5\n5\n5\n5\nsin\nsin\n5\n5\n8\n8\n+\n−\n⇒\n=\nM1\n20\n64\n=\nA1\n5\n4\n=\nAG\nMETHOD 2\nA1\n,\n3π\n4π\nsin\n,sin\n5\n5\nroots of quartic are\nπ\n2π\nsin\n,sin\n5\n5\nattempt to set product of roots equal to\n5\n16\n±\nM1\nπ\n2π\n3π\n4π\n5\nsin\nsin\nsin\nsin\n5\n5\n5\n5\n16\n=\nA1\nrecognition that\nπ\n4π\nsin\nsin\n5\n5\n=\nand\n2π\n3π\nsin\nsin\n5\n5\n=\n2\n2\nπ\n3π\n5\nsin\nsin\n5\n5\n16\n=\nA1\nπ\n3π\n5\nsin\nsin\n5\n5\n4\n=\nAG\ncontinued…\n– 28 –\n8823 – 7106M\nQuestion 12 continued\nMETHOD 3\nConsider\n4\n2\n16sin\n20sin\n5\n0\nθ\nθ\n−\n+\n=\nas a quadratic in\n2\nsin θ\nM1\nare roots of the quadratic.\nA1\nand\n2 3π\nsin\n5\n(\nπ 3π\n,\n5\n5\nθ =\nare roots), so\n2 π\nsin 5\nConsider product of roots:\nM1\n2\n2\nπ\n3π\n5\nsin\nsin\n5\n5\n16\n⇒\n=\nA1\nπ\n3π\n5\nsin\nsin\n5\n5\n4\n=\nAG\n[7 marks]\nTotal [17 marks]",
